# Labels / i18n rules

## Source of truth on disk

- All user-facing strings (labels, tooltips, titles, messages, button text) are **defined only** in modules under `KDB3/js/core/config/labels/`.
- Do not introduce or edit label text in feature code, renderers, or ad-hoc config files outside that directory.

## Wiring to `_KDB.config.labels`

- During bootstrap / config initialization — before any feature reads labels — a dedicated loader (or the labels modules themselves) must assemble the full tree and assign it to `_KDB.config.labels` in one deterministic step (or merge in a single orchestrated place). After that step, treat `_KDB.config.labels` as read-only for the session.
- Feature code must not assign into `_KDB.config.labels.*` at runtime.

## Single source at runtime

- After init, `_KDB.config.labels.*` is the lookup tree the app uses; it must reflect exactly what was loaded from `KDB3/js/core/config/labels/`.
- Feature code reads strings; never hardcodes them.
- Categorize in the on-disk tree (and thus under `_KDB.config.labels`) per UI area, e.g. `tooltips.drillthrough`, `messages.welcome`, `buttons.save`, consistent between files under `labels/` and the resulting `_KDB.config.labels` shape.

## Language keys

- Each label entry is an object keyed by language code: `de`, `en`.
- Other languages are out of scope for now.

```js
// Example shape after load — typically built from modules under js/core/config/labels/
_KDB.config.labels.tooltips.drillthrough = {
  de: "Hier klicken um den Wert im PKZ-AT detaillierter betrachten zu können.",
  en: "Click here to view the value in PKZ-AT in more detail."
};
```

## Active language

- The active language is read from `_KDB.config.language` (e.g. `"de"` or `"en"`).
- Feature code looks up strings via a helper: `_KDB.generalFunctions.label(_KDB, "tooltips.drillthrough")` returns the string in the active language.
- The helper falls back to `de` if the active language has no entry.

## AI translation responsibility

When a sub-chat introduces a new user-facing string OR encounters an existing German-only string while editing:

1. The German text is the source of truth (existing project content is in German).
2. The sub-chat MUST add or update the entry under `KDB3/js/core/config/labels/` (not inline in feature code) and ensure the loaded result includes both `de` and `en` for new or modified labels. No `de`-only entries are allowed for new or modified labels.
3. Translation quality is the sub-chat's responsibility — no machine-translation placeholders, no `"TODO translate"`.

## What is NOT a label

Strings used in technical contexts are NOT labels and stay inline:

- log messages (`fLog("e", "doStuff failed", ...)`)
- error keys / internal codes
- CSS class names
- DOM ids
- event names
- AMD module paths

If in doubt: would a translator ever see this string in production UI? If yes → label in `KDB3/js/core/config/labels/` and on `_KDB.config.labels`. If no → inline.

## Forbidden

- Hardcoded user-facing strings in feature code.
- Defining label text outside `KDB3/js/core/config/labels/` (except the single bootstrap/loader step that attaches to `_KDB.config.labels`).
- Single-language label entries for new/modified labels.
- Reading raw `_KDB.config.labels.*` outside the helper — always go through `_KDB.generalFunctions.label(...)` so language-fallback stays centralized.
